  "readmeFile": "README.nuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.0.1:\n- New package icon: a pair of brackets around a single element\n\nv3.0.0:\n- BREAKING: NonEmptyList<T> no longer inherits List<T>. It wraps its storage, so the non-empty guarantee now holds through IList<T>, ICollection<T> and IList as well\n- BREAKING: Prepend(item) now returns a new list (LINQ semantics); use AddFirst(item) to insert in place\n- BREAKING: Remove(item) returns bool like List<T>; AsReadOnly returns ReadOnlyCollection<T>\n- BREAKING: Dropped .NET 6 target; now targets .NET 8, 9 and 10\n- Collection expressions: NonEmptyList<int> xs = [1, 2, 3]; (also ImmutableNonEmptyList, ConstrainedList, NonEmptySet)\n- List patterns and range slicing: xs is [var head, .. var rest], xs[1..]\n- Type-preserving LINQ: Select, SelectMany, OrderBy/ThenBy, GroupBy, Distinct, Union, Concat, Chunk, Min, Max stay non-empty; query syntax supported\n- Generic math: Sum, Product, Average, Median, Mode, MinMax with no empty-sequence exception path\n- ISpanParsable / TypeConverter: bind NonEmptyList<T> and NonEmptyString directly from query strings, route values and configuration\n- Validation<T, TError>: error-accumulating validation whose error list is non-empty by construction\n- Constraint algebra: ConstrainedList<T, AtLeast<Two>>, Distinct, Sorted, AtMost, Exactly, And, Or; Second()/Third() only when the type proves them\n- New types: NonEmptySet, NonEmptyDictionary, NonEmptyString, NonEmptySpan, NonEmptyZipper, History, EventStream, NonEmptyTree, NonEmptyEnumerable (lazy, infinite)\n- Async batching: BatchNonEmpty (size and time based), ReadAllBatchesAsync for channels, ToNonEmptyAsync / NonEmptyAsyncEnumerable\n- Bundled Roslyn analyzers (NEL001-NEL005) with code fixes, and the [NonEmptyCollection] source generator for domain collections\n- Protected invariant hooks (EnsureMutable, ValidateItem, ValidateRange, ValidateReplacement, ValidateCount) for derived types\n- New factories: NonEmptyList.Of, Create, Range, Iterate, Unfold; FromSpan; params ReadOnlySpan constructors; IEnumerable constructors\n- New operators: Scan, Tails, Inits, Append, Flatten, Unzip, Interleave, Cycle, ConvertAll\n- [NotNullWhen(true)] on TryFrom; DebuggerDisplay and debugger type proxy; O(n) MinBy/MaxBy",
